  ],
  "details": "<p>The house was excavated in 1913 and 1914. The name\u00a0L. Ceius Secundus is mentioned in a painted campaign message on the house's facade. The duovir\u00a0L. Ceius Secundus was the presumed owner of the House of the Ceii.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "A Roman house in Pompeii (I, 6, 15), also known as the House of L. Ceius Secundus. It is also referred to as the House of Fabia and Tyrannus.",
